    <briefdescription>
<para>Returns a &quot;realistic&quot; mean surface height field. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns realistic mountains on a latitude-longtude grid. The returned field is the mean topography for the given grid boxes. Computed using a conserving area-weighted interpolation. The current input data set is the 1/6 degree Navy mean topography.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>blon</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The longitude (in radians) at grid box boundaries. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>blat</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The latitude (in radians) at grid box boundaries. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>zmean</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The mean surface height (meters). The size of this field must be size(blon)-1 by size(blat)-1. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A logical value of TRUE is returned if the surface height field was successfully created. A value of FALSE may be returned if the input topography data set was not readable.</para></simplesect>
<linebreak/>
Example usage: <programlisting filename=".F90"><codeline><highlight class="normal">flag<sp/>=<sp/>get_topog_mean(<sp/>blon,<sp/>blat,<sp/>zmean<sp/>)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
